  <refsect1>
    <title>Description</title>

    <para>The <constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_…()</constant> macros are used to describe the structure and contents
    of a JSON variant to construct with
    <citerefentry><refentrytitle>sd_json_build</refentrytitle><manvolnum>3</manvolnum></citerefentry> and
    related calls. Each macro expands to a type identifier followed by its arguments, cast to the precise
    types the builder expects. They may only be used in the variadic argument list of these calls, and
    there is no type checking beyond what the casts provide.</para>

    <para>A description consists of exactly one value. Values are generated by the macros listed under
    "Values" below, or by <constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_OBJECT()</constant> or
    <constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_ARRAY()</constant>, which in turn take a list of fields or values, and may be
    nested arbitrarily.</para>

    <refsect2>
      <title>Containers</title>

      <variablelist>
        <varlistentry>
          <term><constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_OBJECT(<replaceable>pair</replaceable>…)</constant></term>

          <listitem><para>Generates a JSON object. Takes a list of zero or more key/value pairs, i.e.
          object fields, each described by <constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_PAIR()</constant>,
          <constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_PAIR_CONDITION()</constant> or one of the
          <constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_PAIR_…()</constant> shortcut macros. The fields are added to the object in
          the order specified. Each key may be used only once in the same object, see
          <citerefentry><refentrytitle>sd_json_variant_new_object</refentrytitle><manvolnum>3</manvolnum></citerefentry>.</para>

          <xi:include href="version-info.xml" xpointer="v257"/></listitem>
        </varlistentry>

        <varlistentry>
          <term><constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_EMPTY_OBJECT</constant></term>

          <listitem><para>Generates an empty JSON object, i.e. <literal>{}</literal>.</para>

          <xi:include href="version-info.xml" xpointer="v257"/></listitem>
        </varlistentry>

        <varlistentry>
          <term><constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_ARRAY(<replaceable>value</replaceable>…)</constant></term>

          <listitem><para>Generates a JSON array. Takes a list of zero or more values, which are added to
          the array in the order specified.</para>

          <xi:include href="version-info.xml" xpointer="v257"/></listitem>
        </varlistentry>

        <varlistentry>
          <term><constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_EMPTY_ARRAY</constant></term>

          <listitem><para>Generates an empty JSON array, i.e. <literal>[]</literal>.</para>

          <xi:include href="version-info.xml" xpointer="v257"/></listitem>
        </varlistentry>
      </variablelist>
    </refsect2>

    <refsect2>
      <title>Object Fields</title>

      <variablelist>
        <varlistentry>
          <term><constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_PAIR(<replaceable>name</replaceable>, <replaceable>value</replaceable>)</constant></term>

          <listitem><para>Generates an object field. Takes the key name as a string, followed by the
          description of exactly one value. May only be used directly inside of
          <constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_OBJECT()</constant> (or <function>sd_json_buildo()</function>).</para>

          <xi:include href="version-info.xml" xpointer="v257"/></listitem>
        </varlistentry>

        <varlistentry>
          <term><constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_PAIR_CONDITION(<replaceable>condition</replaceable>, <replaceable>name</replaceable>, <replaceable>value</replaceable>)</constant></term>

          <listitem><para>Similar to <constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_PAIR()</constant>, but takes an additional
          boolean condition as first argument. If false, the field is omitted from the generated object. In
          this case the value is not generated either, with one exception: a JSON string specified with
          <constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_LITERAL()</constant> is parsed even if the field is suppressed, and parse
          errors are reported. Note that a field omitted this way does not count when checking for duplicate
          keys, which allows multiple fields of the same name with mutually exclusive conditions.</para>

          <xi:include href="version-info.xml" xpointer="v257"/></listitem>
        </varlistentry>

        <varlistentry>
          <term><constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_PAIR_STRING()</constant></term>
          <term><constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_PAIR_INTEGER()</constant></term>
          <term><constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_PAIR_UNSIGNED()</constant></term>
          <term><constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_PAIR_REAL()</constant></term>
          <term><constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_PAIR_BOOLEAN()</constant></term>
          <term><constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_PAIR_ARRAY()</constant></term>
          <term><constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_PAIR_EMPTY_ARRAY()</constant></term>
          <term><constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_PAIR_OBJECT()</constant></term>
          <term><constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_PAIR_EMPTY_OBJECT()</constant></term>
          <term><constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_PAIR_NULL()</constant></term>
          <term><constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_PAIR_VARIANT()</constant></term>
          <term><constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_PAIR_VARIANT_ARRAY()</constant></term>
          <term><constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_PAIR_LITERAL()</constant></term>
          <term><constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_PAIR_STRV()</constant></term>
          <term><constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_PAIR_BASE64()</constant></term>
          <term><constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_PAIR_BASE32HEX()</constant></term>
          <term><constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_PAIR_HEX()</constant></term>
          <term><constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_PAIR_OCTESCAPE()</constant></term>
          <term><constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_PAIR_BYTE_ARRAY()</constant></term>
          <term><constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_PAIR_ID128()</constant></term>
          <term><constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_PAIR_UUID()</constant></term>
          <term><constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_PAIR_CALLBACK()</constant></term>

          <listitem><para>Shortcuts that combine <constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_PAIR()</constant> with the value
          macro of the same suffix: they take the key name as first argument, followed by the arguments of
          the respective value macro. For example,
          <constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_PAIR_STRING("foo", "bar")</constant> is equivalent to
          <constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_PAIR("foo", SD_JSON_BUILD_STRING("bar"))</constant>, and
          <constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_PAIR_EMPTY_ARRAY("foo")</constant> is equivalent to
          <constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_PAIR("foo", SD_JSON_BUILD_EMPTY_ARRAY)</constant>.</para>

          <xi:include href="version-info.xml" xpointer="v257"/></listitem>
        </varlistentry>
      </variablelist>
    </refsect2>

    <refsect2>
      <title>Values</title>

      <variablelist>
        <varlistentry>
          <term><constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_STRING(<replaceable>s</replaceable>)</constant></term>

          <listitem><para>Generates a JSON string from a NUL-terminated C string, which must be valid UTF-8.
          If <replaceable>s</replaceable> is <constant>NULL</constant>, a JSON <constant>null</constant>
          value is generated instead.</para>

          <xi:include href="version-info.xml" xpointer="v257"/></listitem>
        </varlistentry>

        <varlistentry>
          <term><constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_INTEGER(<replaceable>i</replaceable>)</constant></term>

          <listitem><para>Generates a JSON number from a signed 64-bit integer.</para>

          <xi:include href="version-info.xml" xpointer="v257"/></listitem>
        </varlistentry>

        <varlistentry>
          <term><constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_UNSIGNED(<replaceable>u</replaceable>)</constant></term>

          <listitem><para>Generates a JSON number from an unsigned 64-bit integer.</para>

          <xi:include href="version-info.xml" xpointer="v257"/></listitem>
        </varlistentry>

        <varlistentry>
          <term><constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_REAL(<replaceable>d</replaceable>)</constant></term>

          <listitem><para>Generates a JSON number from a <type>double</type>.</para>

          <xi:include href="version-info.xml" xpointer="v257"/></listitem>
        </varlistentry>

        <varlistentry>
          <term><constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_BOOLEAN(<replaceable>b</replaceable>)</constant></term>

          <listitem><para>Generates a JSON boolean. Any non-zero value of <replaceable>b</replaceable>
          results in <constant>true</constant>, zero in <constant>false</constant>.</para>

          <xi:include href="version-info.xml" xpointer="v257"/></listitem>
        </varlistentry>

        <varlistentry>
          <term><constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_NULL</constant></term>

          <listitem><para>Generates a JSON <constant>null</constant> value.</para>

          <xi:include href="version-info.xml" xpointer="v257"/></listitem>
        </varlistentry>

        <varlistentry>
          <term><constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_VARIANT(<replaceable>v</replaceable>)</constant></term>

          <listitem><para>Inserts an existing <type>sd_json_variant</type> object, which may be of any type.
          A new reference to the object is taken, the caller's reference is not consumed. If
          <replaceable>v</replaceable> is <constant>NULL</constant>, a JSON <constant>null</constant> value
          is generated instead.</para>

          <xi:include href="version-info.xml" xpointer="v257"/></listitem>
        </varlistentry>

        <varlistentry>
          <term><constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_VARIANT_ARRAY(<replaceable>v</replaceable>, <replaceable>n</replaceable>)</constant></term>

          <listitem><para>Generates a JSON array from a C array of <replaceable>n</replaceable>
          <type>sd_json_variant</type> objects, see
          <function>sd_json_variant_new_array()</function>.</para>

          <xi:include href="version-info.xml" xpointer="v257"/></listitem>
        </varlistentry>

        <varlistentry>
          <term><constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_LITERAL(<replaceable>l</replaceable>)</constant></term>

          <listitem><para>Parses the specified string as JSON (with the same rules as
          <citerefentry><refentrytitle>sd_json_parse</refentrytitle><manvolnum>3</manvolnum></citerefentry>)
          and inserts the result. If <replaceable>l</replaceable> is <constant>NULL</constant>, a JSON
          <constant>null</constant> value is generated instead.</para>

          <xi:include href="version-info.xml" xpointer="v257"/></listitem>
        </varlistentry>

        <varlistentry>
          <term><constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_STRV(<replaceable>l</replaceable>)</constant></term>

          <listitem><para>Generates a JSON array of strings from a <constant>NULL</constant>-terminated C
          string array. If <replaceable>l</replaceable> is <constant>NULL</constant> or empty, an empty
          array is generated.</para>

          <xi:include href="version-info.xml" xpointer="v257"/></listitem>
        </varlistentry>

        <varlistentry>
          <term><constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_BASE64(<replaceable>p</replaceable>, <replaceable>n</replaceable>)</constant></term>
          <term><constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_BASE32HEX(<replaceable>p</replaceable>, <replaceable>n</replaceable>)</constant></term>
          <term><constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_HEX(<replaceable>p</replaceable>, <replaceable>n</replaceable>)</constant></term>
          <term><constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_OCTESCAPE(<replaceable>p</replaceable>, <replaceable>n</replaceable>)</constant></term>

          <listitem><para>Generate a JSON string from the binary data of <replaceable>n</replaceable> bytes
          at <replaceable>p</replaceable>, encoded in Base64, in Base32 with the "Extended Hex" alphabet
          (without padding), in lowercase hexadecimal, or with C-style octal escapes (e.g.
          <literal>\033</literal>) for all bytes that are not printable ASCII characters as well as for
          backslashes and double quotes, respectively. <replaceable>p</replaceable> may be
          <constant>NULL</constant> if <replaceable>n</replaceable> is zero.</para>

          <xi:include href="version-info.xml" xpointer="v257"/></listitem>
        </varlistentry>

        <varlistentry>
          <term><constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_BYTE_ARRAY(<replaceable>p</replaceable>, <replaceable>n</replaceable>)</constant></term>

          <listitem><para>Generates a JSON array of numbers in the range 0…255 from the binary data of
          <replaceable>n</replaceable> bytes at <replaceable>p</replaceable>, one element per byte.
          <replaceable>p</replaceable> may be <constant>NULL</constant> if <replaceable>n</replaceable> is
          zero.</para>

          <xi:include href="version-info.xml" xpointer="v257"/></listitem>
        </varlistentry>

        <varlistentry>
          <term><constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_ID128(<replaceable>id</replaceable>)</constant></term>
          <term><constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_UUID(<replaceable>id</replaceable>)</constant></term>

          <listitem><para>Generate a JSON string from a 128-bit ID, formatted as 32 lowercase hexadecimal
          characters, or in the RFC 9562 UUID format (with dashes), respectively. Note that the address of
          <replaceable>id</replaceable> is taken, hence it must be an lvalue.</para>

          <xi:include href="version-info.xml" xpointer="v257"/></listitem>
        </varlistentry>

        <varlistentry>
          <term><constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_CALLBACK(<replaceable>c</replaceable>, <replaceable>userdata</replaceable>)</constant></term>

          <listitem><para>Invokes the callback <replaceable>c</replaceable> to generate the value. The
          callback is passed a pointer to the variant to return in its <parameter>ret</parameter> argument,
          and the <parameter>userdata</parameter> pointer specified in the macro. If the value is generated
          for an object field, the field's key name is passed in <parameter>name</parameter>. The callback
          should return a negative errno-style error code on failure, which is propagated to the caller of
          <function>sd_json_build()</function>, and a non-negative value on success. If the callback leaves
          <parameter>ret</parameter> unset (i.e. <constant>NULL</constant>), or if <replaceable>c</replaceable>
          is <constant>NULL</constant>, a JSON <constant>null</constant> value is generated. The callback is
          not invoked for fields suppressed with
          <constant>SD_JSON_BUILD_PAIR_CONDITION()</constant>.</para>

          <xi:include href="version-info.xml" xpointer="v257"/></listitem>
        </varlistentry>
      </variablelist>
    </refsect2>
  </refsect1>

  <refsect1>
    <title>Examples</title>

    <example>
      <title>Nested description</title>

      <programlisting>sd_id128_t id = …;
char **tags = …;
const uint8_t data[] = { 1, 2, 3 };
_cleanup_(sd_json_variant_unrefp) sd_json_variant *v = NULL;
int r;

r = sd_json_build(
                &amp;v,
                SD_JSON_BUILD_OBJECT(
                                SD_JSON_BUILD_PAIR("name", SD_JSON_BUILD_STRING("foo")),
                                SD_JSON_BUILD_PAIR_ID128("id", id),
                                SD_JSON_BUILD_PAIR_STRV("tags", tags),
                                SD_JSON_BUILD_PAIR_BASE64("data", data, sizeof(data)),
                                SD_JSON_BUILD_PAIR_CONDITION(tags &amp;&amp; tags[0], "firstTag", SD_JSON_BUILD_STRING(tags[0])),
                                SD_JSON_BUILD_PAIR_ARRAY("values",
                                                         SD_JSON_BUILD_UNSIGNED(4711),
                                                         SD_JSON_BUILD_REAL(0.5),
                                                         SD_JSON_BUILD_NULL),
                                SD_JSON_BUILD_PAIR_LITERAL("extra", "{\"a\":[1,2,3]}")));
if (r &lt; 0)
        return r;</programlisting>
    </example>
  </refsect1>

